# An identifier must be the same in every feature set
law identifier_feature_independent
kind audit
claim the package is built once per feature set and each build reports the identifier it carries
claim every build must report the same identifier; one feature set is not evidence of independence
source ALICE-Physics tests/physics_semantics_id.rs:552 (the identifier is pinned and independent of features)

x-input builds list of record(features: list of text, id: optional text)
x-metric builds = number of builds reported
x-metric feature_sets = number of distinct feature sets (a feature set is unordered; duplicates collapse)
x-metric distinct_identifiers = number of distinct identifiers; unmeasured when any build has no id
# when builds does not match its type (one malformed build is enough), none of the three is measured
x-at-least feature_sets 2     # fewer than 2 distinct feature sets gives no evidence for feature_sets

begin audit
audit identifier-feature-independent
evidence builds
evidence feature_sets
expect distinct_identifiers == 1
end audit

verdict the verdict of the audit block for the derived measurements
